# Amiberry 680x0 CPU / JIT (hosted by Cockatrice III)

This directory is a trimmed copy of [Amiberry](https://github.com/BlitterStudio/amiberry)
(`src/` CPU interpreter, FPU, JIT for ARM64 and x86-64, plus the headers
those units include). It is not a full Amiberry emulator tree.

Copied at commit `cf365446`. Extra CPUEMU cores (`cpuemu_11`–`35`) and
`cpummu.cpp` / `cpummu30.cpp` are included so `newcpu.cpp` type-checks the
cycle-exact and MMU accessors; runtime still uses `cpuemu_0` or JIT.

Cockatrice Mac adapters live here:

- `hosted/` — include overlays (no Amiga chipset) and `amiberry_host.cpp` / `amiberry_memory.cpp`
- `amiberry_glue.cpp` — Basilisk `CPUEngine` for prefs `cpu_emulator uae`
- `sysconfig.h` — CPUEMU_0/11–35/40/50 plus MMUEMU so newcpu.cpp type-checks;
  debugger/savestate/autoconfig stay off. Runtime uses `cpuemu_0` or JIT.

`jit true` uses `src/jit/arm` on ARM64 and `src/jit/x86` on amd64.
`jit false` uses the `cpuemu_0.cpp` interpreter.
